	(text "Battery retention is only needed for\nthe RTC. The rest of the NVSRAM data is\nbacked up in the flash on the RP2350B."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.814 204.216 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0ad7d5cc-596c-4fd8-b7e5-64ae2425c4f3")
	)
	(text "LSB!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 159.258 81.788 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "26111e3e-bdac-454c-9c5b-989a5ac4acc6")
	)
	(text "When this board is plugged in the scope,\nonly connect the Core2350B to USB with the\nUSB connector on this board, not with the\nUSB extension board + flex cable that comes\nwith the Core2350B."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 22.352 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2fa4bc21-e298-4d77-acbc-37304b661bd3")
	)
	(text "D0 should have been \nattached to GPIO7\nand D7 to GPIO0. \nSW or PIO must do a\nbit reversal to get\nthe right value."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.954 71.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "388a373d-db23-4a23-b1ce-ed2b0fad36ea")
	)
	(text "LSB!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 159.258 79.248 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4a733efd-ee31-4b58-8c2c-7b6b173be1ae")
	)
	(text "Core2350 is either powered from VBUS or connector 5V,\nbut we don't want it start unless the 3V3 is active on the\nconnector, to avoid backdriving into the scope when\nUSB is plugged in but the scope is powered off to\navoid latchup.\n\nThe JP8 is closed by default to make sure\nthat RP2350 doesn't get accidentally switched on. \n\nThe JP7 on the OR'ed 5V is to measure power."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 355.346 85.852 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "556cbcde-bd5e-4e85-b8a6-99307e101216")
	)
	(text "3V3 is generated on the Core2350,\nso this is an output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.818 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "81d21172-05f1-47fc-a49b-87a4187245d0")
	)
	(text "MSB!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 159.512 61.468 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "904b16fa-9c6f-4e60-b333-6b1b34b03f0f")
	)
	(text "Put a jumper on J2\nbetween pins 1 and 2\nto use the PCB when a\nUSB cable is plugged in\nbut the board is not\nplugged into the scope."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 298.704 126.746 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "938e774c-76f6-410c-8823-6ecab44273a9")
	)
	(text "The Core2350 has a 100k \npullup to 5V on 3V3_EN. With\na 200k to ground, the 5V gets\nreduced to 3.3V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 383.286 113.284 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9793f8c5-03c6-4690-a3ca-2408d308ecdc")
	)
	(text "BDM_HRESET on the MCP860 is bidirection and\nopen drain. GPIO39 is also connected to an LED on the\nCore2350B. Reset is active low. This circuit\nredrives HRESET and makes it active high on the \nCore2350B side."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.988 167.894 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a820b59f-f6b3-4c8e-acd0-a186c7e66e6e")
	)
	(text "R13 can be used by SW to\ndetect the difference between\nv1 and v2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c07628e8-c41f-47f2-bf79-cb5fca3392f7")
	)
	(text "MSB!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 159.512 107.188 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e6f3d33a-4d9b-4b41-929e-1ee8a3315512")
	)
	(text "BDM_SRESET is not needed: it gets asserted inside the CPU \nwhen HRESET is asserted.\n\nnTA has a scope-side pullup."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.638 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f424eb3b-2628-408c-8b56-f1bc6f60759d")
	)
	(text "This is a PCB \"connector\", not the expensive\nConnectivity AMP Connectors 1-1734099-0.\nThe pinout is different the real connector\nso that we can reuse a standard SAMTEC footprint."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 61.468 21.844 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f6f1f469-c59b-4b7d-9ec6-039ed84caca2")
	)
